OSPF Routing Configuration Lab
Objective

Configure OSPF between Cisco routers and verify neighbor adjacency using both the network statement method and interface-based OSPF configuration.

Topology
R1 ---------------- R2
E0/0              E0/0

192.168.10.1/30   192.168.10.2/30


R3 ---------------- R4
E0/1              E0/0

192.168.20.1/30   192.168.20.2/30

Router 1 Configuration
enable
configure terminal

interface e0/0
 ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
exit

router ospf 1
 router-id 1.1.1.1
 network 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 0

end

Verification
show ip interface brief
show ip ospf
show ip ospf neighbor

Router 2 Configuration
enable
configure terminal

interface e0/0
 ip address 192.168.10.2 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
exit

router ospf 2
 router-id 2.2.2.2
 network 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 0

end

Verification
show ip interface brief
show ip ospf
show ip ospf neighbor

Router 3 Configuration (Interface-Based OSPF)
enable
configure terminal

interface e0/1
 ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
 ip ospf 1 area 0
 ip ospf network point-to-point
exit

router ospf 1
 router-id 3.3.3.3

end

Verification
ping 192.168.20.2

show ip ospf
show ip ospf neighbor

Router 4 Configuration (Interface-Based OSPF)
enable
configure terminal

interface e0/0
 ip address 192.168.20.2 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
 ip ospf 2 area 0
 ip ospf network point-to-point
exit

router ospf 2
 router-id 4.4.4.4

end

Verification
ping 192.168.20.1

show ip ospf
show ip ospf neighbor

Verification Commands
show ip interface brief
show ip ospf
show ip ospf neighbor
show running-config | section ospf

Expected Result
Neighbor ID     State
1.1.1.1         FULL
2.2.2.2         FULL
3.3.3.3         FULL
4.4.4.4         FULL


Successful OSPF adjacency formation indicates that routers are exchanging routing information dynamically.

Key Learnings
OSPF is a link-state routing protocol.
OSPF uses unique Router IDs to identify routers.
OSPF process IDs do not need to match between routers.
Interfaces must be operational (up/up) before OSPF neighbors can form.
Neighbor state FULL indicates successful adjacency.
OSPF can be configured using:
Network statements
Interface-based commands (ip ospf area)
